1
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:01,740
These wheels are square.

2
00:00:01,740 --> 00:00:02,840
So why isn't

3
00:00:02,840 --> 00:00:04,060
the ride bumpy?

4
00:00:04,060 --> 00:00:05,360
On a flat road,

5
00:00:05,360 --> 00:00:06,260
the axle climbs

6
00:00:06,260 --> 00:00:07,460
and drops as each

7
00:00:07,460 --> 00:00:09,040
corner turns over.

8
00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:09,600
Now...

9
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:11,540
change the road.

10
00:00:11,540 --> 00:00:12,720
These curved sections

11
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:13,820
are shaped to match

12
00:00:13,820 --> 00:00:15,220
the square, keeping

13
00:00:15,220 --> 00:00:15,680
its center

14
00:00:15,680 --> 00:00:16,640
at the same height

15
00:00:16,640 --> 00:00:17,720
as it rolls.

16
00:00:17,720 --> 00:00:20,290
The road does the smoothing.

17
00:00:20,290 --> 00:00:21,530
Real square wheel

18
00:00:21,530 --> 00:00:23,270
demonstrations use this idea;

19
00:00:23,270 --> 00:00:24,490
the curve is called

20
00:00:24,490 --> 00:00:26,130
an inverted catenary.

21
00:00:26,130 --> 00:00:27,470
It still takes energy

22
00:00:27,470 --> 00:00:28,090
to move,

23
00:00:28,090 --> 00:00:29,090
and the wheel size

24
00:00:29,090 --> 00:00:30,270
has to match the road.

25
00:00:30,270 --> 00:00:32,070
The surprise isn't

26
00:00:32,070 --> 00:00:33,670
that squares became circles.

27
00:00:33,670 --> 00:00:34,790
It's that the road

28
00:00:34,790 --> 00:00:35,330
was part

29
00:00:35,330 --> 00:00:37,033
of the machine.

